   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public officers law, in relation to the qualifications for\nholding the office of assistant county attorney in the county of Herkimer",
    "basePrintNo": "S9128",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9128-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Public Officers Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9128\n\nSPONSOR: WALCZYK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public officers law, in relation to the qualifica-\ntions for holding the office of assistant county attorney in the county\nof Herkimer\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo waive the residency requirement for the Herkimer County Assistant\nAttorney.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1-Amends section 3 of the public officers law is amended by\nadding a new subdivision 73, which waives the residency requirement for\nHerkimer County Assistant Attorney, provided that\n\nSection 2 - Provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe County of Herkimer currently has limited flexibility to fill the\nposition of Assistant County Attorney due to a residency requirement.  A\nResolution was adopted at the county level which would expand the resi-\ndency requirement by asking the state to act on waiving this requirement\nproviding that the candidate reside in an adjoining county. This is\nparticularly important for Herkimer County at a time when hiring and\nmaintaining staff remains a challenge.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
